WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.237
Sparrow: Whew! It is so hot here!

2
00:00:03.238 --> 00:00:06.612
I have been flying over this desert all day.

3
00:00:06.613 --> 00:00:09.612
I need to find a cool place to rest. Look,

4
00:00:09.613 --> 00:00:24.822
there's a hole in the ground. I'll rest there. Mouse:

5
00:00:24.823 --> 00:00:27.781
Who are you? Sparrow:

6
00:00:27.782 --> 00:00:31.414
Oh, I'm sorry. I am a sparrow.

7
00:00:31.415 --> 00:00:37.784
This desert is so dry and hot that I did not expect to see any animals living here!

8
00:00:37.785 --> 00:00:43.899
Mouse: I am a desert mouse, and there are a lot of animals

9
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.242
here. Sparrow:

10
00:00:45.243 --> 00:00:50.619
Really? Mouse: Yes. The days are very hot and dry, but the nights are

11
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.837
cold. So most desert animals do not move around during the

12
00:00:54.838 --> 00:00:58.168
day. Sparrow: But how do they endure so

13
00:00:58.169 --> 00:01:02.723
much heat? It is so hot that I am about to

14
00:01:02.724 --> 00:01:08.062
die! Mouse: Well, some desert animals use parts of their bodies to

15
00:01:08.063 --> 00:01:16.378
cool off. For example, desert owls open their mouths wide and flutter

16
00:01:16.379 --> 00:01:20.474
their throats. The jackrabbit's ears are long and have many blood

17
00:01:20.475 --> 00:01:24.678
vessels. The heat is released through the blood vessels in its long

18
00:01:24.679 --> 00:01:28.629
ears. Sparrow: Oh, that's

19
00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:33.827
interesting! Up north, I have seen other rabbits, and their ears are much

20
00:01:33.828 --> 00:01:39.158
shorter. Mouse: Yes, up north, they do not need long ears

21
00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:43.912
to survive. All over the world, animals are suited to their different

22
00:01:43.913 --> 00:01:47.710
habitats. For example, most desert animals are

23
00:01:47.711 --> 00:01:51.606
light-colored. Their lighter colors keep them from getting really hot too.

24
00:01:51.607 --> 00:01:54.637
Sparrow: Then what about the darker

25
00:01:54.638 --> 00:01:59.380
animals? They would get much hotter than light-colored animals. Right?

26
00:01:59.381 --> 00:02:05.111
Mouse: You are right. Vultures are dark-colored, but they wet their legs with their

27
00:02:05.112 --> 00:02:07.783
urine. The urine cools the blood in their

28
00:02:07.784 --> 00:02:10.635
legs. The cooler blood goes back through their bodies.

29
00:02:10.636 --> 00:02:16.726
Sparrow: I see. They are really amazing!

30
00:02:16.727 --> 00:02:20.311
Then how do desert animals find water?

31
00:02:20.312 --> 00:02:22.791
You do need water, don't you? Mouse:

32
00:02:22.792 --> 00:02:28.709
Of course! We desert creatures get water from plants.

33
00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:32.202
The juicy cactus is a favorite! Have a piece! Sparrow:

34
00:02:32.203 --> 00:02:35.811
But won't I get stuck by the thorns?

35
00:02:35.812 --> 00:02:41.720
Mouse: Not really. Go ahead, just be careful.

36
00:02:41.721 --> 00:02:49.365
Sparrow: Hmm, not bad! By the way, how do you stay cool in this

37
00:02:49.366 --> 00:02:52.300
desert? Mouse: I live in an underground den

38
00:02:52.301 --> 00:02:54.982
like this. I close the opening when it is very

39
00:02:54.983 --> 00:02:56.653
hot. That keeps out the

40
00:02:56.654 --> 00:02:59.573
heat. Then I can save the moisture from my

41
00:02:59.574 --> 00:03:05.190
breath. Sparrow: Wonderful! Desert animals are really

42
00:03:05.191 --> 00:03:07.385
amazing. But I might not survive

43
00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:11.200
here. Mouse: That's true. The desert gets very little

44
00:03:11.201 --> 00:03:14.927
rain. It gets less than 25 centimeters of rain a

45
00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:19.427
year! So all the animals in the desert have special ways to help them

46
00:03:19.428 --> 00:03:21.049
survive. But you have wings.

47
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:25.723
You can fly to a place where you will survive well.

48
00:03:25.724 --> 00:03:27.488
Sparrow: Yes, you are right!

49
00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:29.225
I have to leave now.

50
00:03:29.226 --> 00:03:33.292
Thank you for telling me about desert animals. Good-bye!

51
00:03:33.293 --> 00:03:36.864
Mouse: My pleasure! Good-bye!

